  <entry xml:lang="en">
    <title>Photo — 2 Sept 2026</title>
    <link href="https://posts.rauljimenez.info/photos/2026/09/01/e4bdf"/>
    <id>https://posts.rauljimenez.info/photos/2026/09/01/e4bdf</id>
    <published>2026-09-01T23:45:16.767Z</published>
    <updated>2026-09-01T23:45:16.767Z</updated>
    <category term="photo"/>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://posts.rauljimenez.info/media/2026/09/img-20260829-114558.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;A photo of me posing: a middle-aged man with graying hair and a short beard smiles warmly in the foreground, looking directly at the camera. He is wearing a pale yellow T-shirt. He is on a solar-powered boat on the Tranco Reservoir in Jaén. Behind him, a vast expanse of deep turquoise water stretches into the distance, with gentle ripples on the surface. On both sides of the water, densely forested hills covered in green pine trees rise up, and in the background, taller, rocky mountains are visible. The sky is bright blue with scattered thin white clouds. The lighting is bright, natural sunlight. The photo is taken from a medium-shot perspective, at eye level.&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Last weekend, I enjoyed a solar-powered boat ride across &amp;quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://maps.app.goo.gl/15NLEqsdjSzi69No9&quot;&gt;Pantano del Tranco&lt;/a&gt;&amp;quot; (Tranco Reservoir) in Cazorla, Jaén Spain 😍🌲⛰️🌊🧘‍♂️&lt;/p&gt;</content>
  </entry>
  <entry xml:lang="en">
    <title>It is beautiful, but very expensive for what it is</title>
    <link href="https://posts.rauljimenez.info/reviews/2026/09/01/it-is-beautiful-but-very"/>
    <id>https://posts.rauljimenez.info/reviews/2026/09/01/it-is-beautiful-but-very</id>
    <published>2026-09-01T22:10:46.806Z</published>
    <updated>2026-09-01T22:10:46.806Z</updated>
    <category term="review"/>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;📝 Reviewed &lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livraria_Lello&quot;&gt;Livraria Lello&lt;/a&gt; — ★★★★☆&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://posts.rauljimenez.info/media/2026/09/livraria-lello.png&quot; alt=&quot;livraria-lello panorama&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;What some people call the “Harry Potter bookstore” is the Lello Bookstore (Livraria Lello), located in the historic center of Porto, Portugal, is very beautiful, but:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We had to wait ~20/30min to get it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And it&apos;s pretty small. I would say around ~350 square meters, divided into 2 floors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://posts.rauljimenez.info/media/2026/09/livraria-lello.png&quot; alt=&quot;livraria-lello panorama&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
  </entry>
